  "sdkPr9": {
    "baseRefName": "codex/platform-receipt-contract",
    "body": "A malformed HTTP-200 GeoNames response was cached as a successful request, so later explicit calls repeated the same failure without refetching. Unsafe table indices could also escape as non-string City fields, and callers could mutate arrays returned by `preload()` to change later searches. Validate the compact v1 index and each requested shard before cache fulfillment, reject malformed data with a fixed schema error, and return metadata snapshots.\n\nThe fix keeps successful/in-flight request sharing, original transport/parser failures and later explicit retry. It preserves the checked-in dataset's Unicode names, empty region/country labels and geographic endpoints. No automatic retry, new endpoint, eager shard loading, host-dependent timezone validation or account/storage change is added. Structurally valid mixed-generation data remains undetectable in v1 and is documented with a counterexample.\n\nThis draft is stacked on SDK #8. New engine `0.1.1-rc.4` has source `d190d97c981c7cacc6eb4ab6a49bdb8451ca3459` and immutable artifact carrier `9ad6a73984e69b897a6422429fab1970a7c89450`; SHA-256 `0146fdff7abb6b937cf4d66b4cdaf0c80ecf238ea71f1f4f9fb27eae687a0d20`. The archive is anonymously downloadable and verified. Site application rc.1 and standalone starter rc.3 pins remain unchanged. SDK #5's explicit **do not merge / do not publish** hold remains; no npm publication, production deployment, required human review or external adoption is claimed.\n\nValidation:\n\n- 496 tests / 30 files on Node 20 and 22. Required workspace lint/typecheck/build, format, checksum, neutrality, TypeDoc, exports, contents and dry-pack gates pass.\n- All 33,934 checked-in rows validate; a fixed 27-query comparison preserves results, metadata and request order. Nine independent strict-unhandled-rejection controls cover retry races, pending work, mutation, coercion, unsafe indices and compatibility.\n- Two clean packed consumers pass public TypeScript imports, schema/transport recovery, mutation isolation and retained calculation/receipt checks; isolated audit reports zero vulnerabilities. All 96 chart comparisons match rc.3 except the reported engine version.\n- Actual Chrome passes 20 packed-consumer checks with intercepted synthetic HTTP responses, all 22 installed files verified, optional/root bundle isolation, no storage, fixed GET resource paths, explicit retry and offline cache reuse. Shard selection still reveals the normalized initial; full query/birth text is not sent in these controls.\n\nEvidence records preserve original failures and harness corrections. Existing SDK CI targets main PRs, so passing stacked-PR CI is not claimed.\n\n[Full evidence](https://github.com/ZodiacsOfficial/sdk/blob/ef846c82dd284559f1574f69ee901a221a7a722a/docs/platform/EVIDENCE.md#geonames-schema-and-cache-integrity-candidate) \u00b7 [Immutable archive](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ZodiacsOfficial/sdk/9ad6a73984e69b897a6422429fab1970a7c89450/artifacts/zodiacs-engine-0.1.1-rc.4.tgz)\n",
